#: ../../../install_osx_src.md:1
msgid "Source Installation on macOS"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_osx_src.md:3
msgid ""
"This tutorial will work for macOS Catalina 10.15, macOS BigSur 10.16, and "
"macOS Monterey 12.0."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_osx_src.md:6
msgid "Install tools"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_osx_src.md:8
msgid ""
"The use of some additional tools is recommended to help with the source "
"compilation, although other ways of correctly getting and building the "
"sources are also possible."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_osx_src.md:11
msgid ""
"The easiest way to get the sources of all libraries is to use [vcstool]"
"(https://github.com/dirk-thomas/vcstool)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_osx_src.md:14
msgid ""
"To compile all the different libraries and gz-sim in the right order [colcon]"
"(https://colcon.readthedocs.io/en/released/) is recommended. The colcon tool "
"is available on all platforms using pip (or pip3, if pip fails)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_osx_src.md:18
msgid "Python3 from homebrew"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_osx_src.md:20
msgid ""
"Tools and dependencies for Garden can be installed using the [homebrew "
"package manager](https://brew.sh/). The homebrew tool can be installed by "
"entering the following in a terminal:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_osx_src.md:23
msgid ""
"/bin/bash -c \"$(curl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Homebrew/"
"install/master/install.sh)\"\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_osx_src.md:27
msgid ""
"Garden is compatible with Python3; it can be installed by running the "
"following in a terminal:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_osx_src.md:29
msgid "brew install python3\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_osx_src.md:33
msgid "vcstool and colcon from pip"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_osx_src.md:35
msgid "PIP is available on all platforms:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_osx_src.md:37
msgid "python3 -m pip install vcstool\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_osx_src.md:41
msgid "python3 -m pip install -U colcon-common-extensions\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_osx_src.md:45
msgid "Getting the sources"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_osx_src.md:47
msgid ""
"The first step is to create a developer workspace in which `vcstool` and "
"`colcon` can work:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_osx_src.md:50
msgid ""
"mkdir -p ~/workspace/src\n"
"cd ~/workspace/src\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_osx_src.md:55
msgid ""
"Use `vcstool` to automatically retrieve all the Gazebo libraries sources "
"from their repositories:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_osx_src.md:58
msgid ""
"vcs import --input https://raw.githubusercontent.com/gazebo-tooling/"
"gazebodistro/master/collection-garden.yaml src\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_osx_src.md:62
msgid "The src subdirectory should contain all the sources ready to be built."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_osx_src.md:65
msgid "Install dependencies"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_osx_src.md:67
msgid "Add `osrf/simulation` to Homebrew formulae"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_osx_src.md:69
msgid ""
"brew update\n"
"brew tap osrf/simulation\n"
"brew trust osrf/simulation\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_osx_src.md:75
msgid "Install all dependencies:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_osx_src.md:77
msgid "Dependency for Ogre:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_osx_src.md:79
msgid "brew install xquartz --cask\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_osx_src.md:83
msgid "General dependencies:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_osx_src.md:85
msgid ""
"brew install assimp boost bullet cmake cppzmq dartsim doxygen eigen fcl "
"ffmpeg flann freeimage freetype gdal gflags google-benchmark gts ipopt "
"jsoncpp libccd libyaml libzzip libzip nlopt ode open-scene-graph ossp-uuid "
"ogre1.9 ogre2.3 pkg-config protobuf qt@5 qwt-qt5 rapidjson ruby tbb tinyxml "
"tinyxml2 urdfdom zeromq\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_osx_src.md:89
msgid ""
"`qt@5` is a \"keg only\" Homebrew formula and its path must be explicitly "
"configured before building Gazebo:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_osx_src.md:91
msgid ""
"# qt@5\n"
"export CMAKE_PREFIX_PATH=${CMAKE_PREFIX_PATH:+$CMAKE_PREFIX_PATH:}`brew --"
"prefix qt@5`\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_osx_src.md:96
msgid "Unlink `qt` to avoid conflicts with other versions of qt (e.g. qt6)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_osx_src.md:98
msgid "brew unlink qt\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_osx_src.md:102
msgid "Install compiler requirements"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_osx_src.md:104
msgid "The Gazebo Libraries require the Xcode 10 compiler on MacOS Mojave."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_osx_src.md:106
msgid ""
"On Mac machines, gcc is acquired by installing Xcode command line tools. The "
"required version of Xcode for Garden is Xcode 10.3, which can be downloaded "
"from [Apple Developer Site](https://developer.apple.com/download/more/). You "
"will need to sign in to your Apple account and download the Mojave version "
"of Xcode command line tools. Command line tools can also be obtained by "
"downloading Xcode from the Apple App Store (installing the full app may take "
"over an hour)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_osx_src.md:113
msgid "Building the Gazebo Libraries in MacOS Catalina (10.15)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_osx_src.md:115
msgid ""
"If you want to compile Gazebo Libraries in MacOS Catalina (10.15) you will "
"need to apply some patches in your filesystem:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_osx_src.md:117
msgid ""
"`/Applications/Xcode.app/Contents/Developer/Platforms/MacOSX.platform/"
"Developer/SDKs/MacOSX10.15.sdk/System/Library/Frameworks/Ruby.framework/"
"Headers/ruby/ruby/intern.h`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_osx_src.md:119
msgid "Create a file called `intern.patch` with the following content:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_osx_src.md:121
msgid ""
"--- intern.h    2019-12-16 18:17:08.000000000 +0100\n"
"+++ /Applications/Xcode.app/Contents/Developer/Platforms/MacOSX.platform/"
"Developer/SDKs/MacOSX10.15.sdk/System/Library/Frameworks/Ruby.framework/"
"Headers/ruby/ruby/intern.h\n"
"@@ -14,6 +14,10 @@\n"
" #ifndef RUBY_INTERN_H\n"
" #define RUBY_INTERN_H 1\n"
"\n"
"+#if __cplusplus > 199711L\n"
"+#define register      // Deprecated in C++11.\n"
"+#endif  // #if __cplusplus > 199711L\n"
"+\n"
" #if defined(__cplusplus)\n"
" extern \"C\" {\n"
" #if 0\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_osx_src.md:137 ../../../install_osx_src.md:161
msgid "Now we can apply the patch:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_osx_src.md:139
msgid "sudo patch -p0 < intern.patch\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_osx_src.md:143
msgid ""
"`/Applications/Xcode.app/Contents/Developer/Platforms/MacOSX.platform/"
"Developer/SDKs/MacOSX10.15.sdk/System/Library/Frameworks/Ruby.framework/"
"Headers/ruby/ruby/config.h`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_osx_src.md:145
msgid "Create a file called `config.patch` with the following content:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_osx_src.md:147
msgid ""
"--- config.h    2019-12-16 18:19:13.000000000 +0100\n"
"+++ /Applications/Xcode.app/Contents/Developer/Platforms/MacOSX.platform/"
"Developer/SDKs/MacOSX10.15.sdk/System/Library/Frameworks/Ruby.framework/"
"Headers/ruby/ruby/config.h\n"
"@@ -410,6 +410,6 @@\n"
" #define RUBY_PLATFORM_CPU \"x86_64\"\n"
" #endif /* defined __x86_64__ &&! defined RUBY_PLATFORM_CPU */\n"
" #define RUBY_PLATFORM_OS \"darwin19\"\n"
"-#define RUBY_ARCH\"universal-\"RUBY_PLATFORM_OS\n"
"-#define RUBY_PLATFORM\"universal.\"RUBY_PLATFORM_CPU\"-\"RUBY_PLATFORM_OS\n"
"+#define RUBY_ARCH \"universal-\" RUBY_PLATFORM_OS\n"
"+#define RUBY_PLATFORM \"universal.\" RUBY_PLATFORM_CPU \"-\" "
"RUBY_PLATFORM_OS\n"
" #endif /* INCLUDE_RUBY_CONFIG_H */\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_osx_src.md:163
msgid "sudo patch -p0 < config.patch\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_osx_src.md:167
msgid "Building the Gazebo Libraries"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_osx_src.md:169
msgid ""
"Once the compiler and all the sources are in place it is time to compile "
"them. Start the procedure by changing into the workspace and listing the "
"packages recognized by `colcon`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_osx_src.md:173
msgid ""
"cd ~/workspace/\n"
"colcon graph\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_osx_src.md:178
msgid ""
"`colcon graph` should list the Gazebo libraries with an [interdependency "
"diagram](https://colcon.readthedocs.io/en/released/reference/verb/graph."
"html#example-output). If that is the case, then you are ready to build the "
"whole set of libraries:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_osx_src.md:183
msgid ""
"colcon build --merge-install\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_osx_src.md:188
msgid ""
"Note if you are on an ARM based Apple Silicon Mac machine, you may need to "
"set a couple more cmake args:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_osx_src.md:190
msgid ""
"colcon build --cmake-args -DCMAKE_MACOSX_RPATH=FALSE -"
"DCMAKE_INSTALL_NAME_DIR=$(pwd)/install/lib --merge-install\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_osx_src.md:194
msgid "To speed up the build process, you could also disable tests by using"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_osx_src.md:196
msgid "colcon build --cmake-args -DBUILD_TESTING=OFF --merge-install\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_osx_src.md:200
msgid ""
"To use debuggers activate debug symbols. Gazebo will run slower, but you'll "
"be able to use `lldb`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_osx_src.md:202
msgid ""
"colcon build --cmake-args ' -DBUILD_TESTING=OFF' ' -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Debug' "
"--merge-install\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_osx_src.md:206
msgid "To build a specific package with all its dependent packages:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_osx_src.md:208
msgid "colcon build --merge-install --packages-up-to PACKAGE_NAME\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_osx_src.md:212
msgid "To build a single package:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_osx_src.md:214
msgid "colcon build --merge-install --packages-select PACKAGE_NAME\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_osx_src.md:218
msgid ""
"Visit [colcon documentation](https://colcon.readthedocs.io/en/released/#) to "
"view more `colcon` build and test options."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_osx_src.md:220
msgid "If there are no errors, all the binaries should be ready to use."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_osx_src.md:222
msgid "Using the workspace"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_osx_src.md:224
msgid "The workspace needs to be sourced every time a new terminal is used."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_osx_src.md:226
msgid "Run the following command to source the workspace in bash:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_osx_src.md:228
msgid ". ~/workspace/install/setup.bash\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_osx_src.md:232
msgid "Or in zsh:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_osx_src.md:234
msgid ". ~/workspace/install/setup.zsh\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_osx_src.md:238
msgid "You should now be able to launch gazebo:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_osx_src.md:240
msgid ""
"# launch server in one terminal\n"
"gz sim -v 4 shapes.sdf -s\n"
"\n"
"# launch gui in a separate terminal\n"
"# remember to source the workspace setup script\n"
"gz sim -v 4 -g\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_osx_src.md:249
msgid ""
"This is the end of the source install instructions; head back to the "
"[Getting started](getstarted) page to start using Gazebo!"
msgstr ""

